An interactive chess system that integrates **Stockfish**, **Lc0**, and **LLMs (e.g., Gemini, LLaMA3)** to generate **real-time, human-like commentary** for every move played. Designed for chess enthusiasts, learners, and analysts.

---

## 🚀 Key Features

- 🧠 **Dual-engine Analysis**: Combines Stockfish (symbolic) + Lc0 (neural) for enriched evaluation.
- 💬 **LLM Commentary**: Uses Gemini (via LangChain) to generate strategic, contextual comments.
- ♟️ **Game Modes**: 
  - User vs User
  - User vs System
  - System vs System
- 🧪 **Evaluation Framework**: BLEU, ROUGE, METEOR, BERTScore, BARTScore, Distinct-n metrics.
- 🧾 **Endgame Summary**: Auto-generated story-like summary at game conclusion.
- 📊 **User Profiles & Stats**: Tracks games, usernames, and personalized commentary tone.

---

## 🗂️ Project Structure
├── DATA/ # Game data and FEN records
├── assets/ # Images, chessboard UI elements
├── metrics/ # Evaluation metric implementations
├── tests/ # Unit tests
├── chess_commentator*.py # Main codebase (variants of core logic)
├── requirements.txt # Required dependencies
├── README.md # Project documentation


---

## 🛠️ How It Works

1. **Pygame Interface** displays the chessboard and allows interaction.
2. **Engines analyze** the move before & after execution.
3. **Features extracted**: evaluation delta, material balance, king safety, etc.
4. **LLM generates commentary** using structured prompts from analysis.
5. **Metrics evaluate** commentary vs reference texts.

---

## 📈 Model Performance (Zero-Shot)

| Metric         | Gemini-1.5 | LLaMA3-70B | Gemma2-9B |
|----------------|------------|------------|-----------|
| BLEU           | 0.3413     | 0.2399     | 0.2344    |
| ROUGE-1-F1     | 0.3671     | 0.3629     | 0.2921    |
| METEOR         | 0.2086     | 0.1814     | 0.1320    |
| BERTScore (F1) | 0.72       | 0.65       | 0.58      |
| Distinct-2     | 0.75       | 0.60       | 0.50      |

> ✅ Gemini-1.5-flash consistently performs best across fluency, relevance, and semantic accuracy.

---

## 🔧 Setup Instructions

### 1. Clone and Install
bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/chess-commentary-ai.git
cd chess-commentary-ai
pip install -r requirements.txt

### 2. Run Main Program
bash
python chess_commentator.py
🎮 Make sure Stockfish & Lc0 binaries are accessible via PATH or configured properly in your script.

📌 Technologies Used
  -Python, Pygame
  -Stockfish, Lc0 (UCI Engines)
  -LangChain, Gemini API, LLaMA3, Gemma2
  -NLTK, sacrebleu, rouge-score, BERTScore, BARTScore

📊 Evaluation Metrics
  -BLEU, ROUGE, METEOR – for n-gram and semantic overlap
  -BERTScore, BARTScore – for contextual alignment and fluency
  -Distinct-2 – for response diversity
  -Qualitative Scores – human annotator judgments (fluency, clarity, etc.)
