webui_1752600276370.py,attached_assets/webui_1752600276370.py,f2e3e397eeb678dbf03fd79ecf97792d20ab756c,breakingcircuits1337/SecurityIntelligence,https://api.github.com/repositories/1030594221/contents/attached_assets/webui_1752600276370.py?ref=707c8524e319d42abcf3bff7823e645137eeba48,https://api.github.com/repositories/1030594221/git/blobs/f2e3e397eeb678dbf03fd79ecf97792d20ab756c,https://github.com/breakingcircuits1337/SecurityIntelligence/blob/707c8524e319d42abcf3bff7823e645137eeba48/attached_assets/webui_1752600276370.py,,,0,0,1,20,2025-08-02T00:23:19Z,1,0,"# SecuriAI Security Testing Dashboard

![Build Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/build-passing-brightgreen.svg)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)

> **Modern AI-powered security platform for automated vulnerability scanning, compliance, and extensibility.**

---

## Features

- **Multi-provider AI integration**: Gemini, Mistral, Groq, with few-shot prompt tuning and real-time LRU caching.
- **Automated security tests**: XSS, SQLi, IDOR, CSRF, DOM-XSS, SQLi PoC (sqlmap in Docker).
- **Network tools**: Ping, traceroute, port scan, DNS lookup.
- **Real-time dashboard**: Live WebSocket updates, progress bars, sparkline charts, vulnerability toasts.
- **Compliance mapping**: Auto-maps findings to OWASP Top 10, PCI-DSS, and SOC 2 controls.
- **Scheduled scans & regression diff**: Cron-based recurring scans, with new/fixed vuln tracking and diff visualization.
- **Plugin marketplace**: WASM scanner/plugin support, drag-and-drop install for community-built tools.
- **Exports & sharing**: PDF/Markdown report export, shareable signed links.
- **Accessibility & dark mode**: Theme toggle, skip links, focus rings, aria-labels.
- **Onboarding**: Guided first-use Radix onboarding tour.

---

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- **Node.js** v20+ and npm
- **Docker** (required for advanced sqlmap testing & plugins)
- (Optional) PostgreSQL if migrating from in-memory storage

### Getting started

```sh
git clone https://github.com/yourorg/securiai.git
cd securiai
npm install
npm run dev
```

- Visit `http://localhost:5000` in your browser.

---

## Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file at project root (or use export):

| Variable        | Description                    | Example                        |
|-----------------|-------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| `SHARE_SECRET`  | JWT signing for share links    | `export SHARE_SECRET=mysupersecret` |
| `GEMINI_API_KEY`| Gemini key (for backend)       | `export GEMINI_API_KEY=sk-...` |
| `MISTRAL_API_KEY`| Mistral key                   | `export MISTRAL_API_KEY=sk-...`|
| `GROQ_API_KEY`  | Groq key                       | `export GROQ_API_KEY=sk-...`   |

---

## Scripts

| Script        | Description                                 |
|---------------|---------------------------------------------|
| `npm run dev` | Start dev server (client & API, hot reload) |
| `npm run build` | Build client (Vite) & server (esbuild)    |
| `npm start`   | Run production build                        |
| `npm test`    | (Reserved for future tests)                 |

---

## Architecture

- **Client**: React 18 + Vite + TailwindCSS + Radix UI.  
    - Key pages: Dashboard, Web Testing, Network Recon, Reports, Schedules, Plugins.
- **Server**: Express + TypeScript  
    - In-memory storage (Postgres-ready via Drizzle schema)
    - Services: SecurityTesting, Scheduler, Plugins, Reporting, Compliance
    - WebSocket server for real-time updates
- **Scheduler**: node-cron for scheduled scans; jobs call SecurityTestingService.
- **Plugin loader**: Loads WASM plugins from `/plugins` dir, registers by manifest/capabilities.
- **Extensibility**: New scanners/parsers can be added as WASM plugins (see below).

```
[ React UI ] <--WS/API--> [ Express API ] --[ Scheduler, Security, Plugins, Storage ]-->
```

---

## Scheduled Scans & Monitoring

- **Create schedule**:  
  POST `/api/schedules` with { targetUrl, testTypes, intensity, cron, aiProviderId }
- **Cron syntax**:  
  `""0 */6 * * *""` (every 6 hours), `""0 0 * * *""` (daily)
- **List schedules**:  
  GET `/api/schedules`
- **Delete**:  
  DELETE `/api/schedules/:id`
- **Regression diff**:  
  After each scheduled scan, new/fixed vulns are calculated and shown in report detail.

---

## Compliance Templates

- Each scan automatically maps findings to:
    - **OWASP Top 10** (e.g. A03 Injection)
    - **PCI-DSS** (e.g. Req. 6.5.1)
    - **SOC 2** Security (e.g. Criteria 6.2)
- Reports/exports include a compliance table (PASS/FAIL per control).

---

## Plugin Development Guide

**Manifest example (plugin.json):**
```json
{
  ""id"": ""domxss-headless"",
  ""name"": ""DOM-XSS Headless Scanner"",
  ""version"": ""1.0.0"",
  ""entry_wasm"": ""plugin.wasm"",
  ""capabilities"": [""scanner""],
  ""description"": ""Scans pages with a headless browser to detect DOM-based XSS.""
}
```

**WASM interface:**
- Export a function: `scan(targetPtr: number, len: number): number`
- Use host functions:
  - `log(msg: string)`
  - `http_fetch(url: string): string`
- Return a pointer to a JSON-encoded array of vulnerabilities.

**Install plugin:**
- Zip plugin directory and upload via Plugins page or POST to `/api/plugins/upload`.

---

## API Cheat-sheet

| Method | Endpoint                          | Description                     |
|--------|-----------------------------------|---------------------------------|
| GET    | /api/ai-providers                 | List AI providers               |
| POST   | /api/ai-providers                 | Add AI provider                 |
| GET    | /api/security-tests               | List security tests             |
| POST   | /api/security-tests               | Start a security test           |
| POST   | /api/security-tests/:id/stop      | Cancel a running test           |
| GET    | /api/schedules                    | List scan schedules             |
| POST   | /api/schedules                    | Add schedule                    |
| DELETE | /api/schedules/:id                | Remove schedule                 |
| GET    | /api/reports                      | List reports                    |
| GET    | /api/reports/:id/export?format=md | Export report as Markdown/PDF   |
| POST   | /api/reports/:id/share            | Generate share link             |
| GET    | /api/plugins                      | List installed plugins          |
| POST   | /api/plugins/upload               | Upload a plugin (admin/dev)     |

---

## Security Notes

- **Rate limiting**: All `/api` routes are protected (express-rate-limit).
- **SSRF safe**: Only public IPv4/IPv6 URLs allowed for scans; localhost/ranges blocked.
- **Plugin sandbox**: WASM plugins run with timeout (25ms) and memory cap (8MB).
- **No credentials stored**: API keys are masked in all client responses.

---

