sample.py,sample.py,1fc6dc68014cdcd80f2364e4eebc0078bb7cfe81,Bhargav3704/Heterogeneous-Cloud-Workloads-with-Cost-Aware-Recommendations,https://api.github.com/repositories/1016448122/contents/sample.py?ref=fb39f5e08aace8e1658f1ccb63a04f20b6ec7833,https://api.github.com/repositories/1016448122/git/blobs/1fc6dc68014cdcd80f2364e4eebc0078bb7cfe81,https://github.com/Bhargav3704/Heterogeneous-Cloud-Workloads-with-Cost-Aware-Recommendations/blob/fb39f5e08aace8e1658f1ccb63a04f20b6ec7833/sample.py,"AI-driven system to optimize heterogeneous cloud workloads using FAISS, LLM agents, SMT tuning, and cost-aware infrastructure recommendations.",,0,0,0,3,2025-07-09T03:23:08Z,0,0,"# 🚀 Heterogeneous Cloud Workloads with Cost-Aware Recommendations

This project is an intelligent cloud infrastructure optimization platform that converts **natural language workload descriptions** into a fully optimized, cost-aware infrastructure blueprint. It leverages a multi-agent architecture powered by **LLMs (LLaMA 3), FAISS semantic retrieval, SMT-aware threading, and machine learning models** to automate decisions for NUMA topology, CPU cores, RAM, storage, bandwidth, and cost projection.

Unlike static cloud advisors like AWS Compute Optimizer or GCP Recommender, this system supports **heterogeneous workload patterns** (CPU-bound, IO-bound, memory-bound, or mixed) and **dynamically reasons** over concurrency levels, performance goals, and application behavior. Each component is independently designed using agentic reasoning, enabling modularity and explainability.

At the core of the system is a **FAISS + Groq-based hybrid workload classifier**, followed by a chain of agents and formulas that estimate each cloud dimension: from NUMA thread layout to RAM sizing, and from storage strategy to bandwidth planning. It then invokes an **XGBoost-trained pricing engine** to match the recommended configuration to a cost-effective AWS EC2 instance and generates a **professional PDF report** for enterprise deployment or decision-making.

This system is ideal for:
- Cloud architects designing scalable deployments
- Enterprises looking for cost optimization
- AI-driven DevOps tooling
- Infrastructure-as-code augmentation

The project was developed during an internship at **Reliance Jio Infocomm** and also forms the foundation of a research paper under submission to **IEEE/Springer**.



## 🧠 Key Features

- **Workload Classification** using FAISS + LLaMA 3 agents  
- **Concurrency Extraction** via LLM reasoning  
- **NUMA & CPU Thread Optimization** (Agent-based + SMT formula fallback)  
- **RAM Estimation** using workload/app-type-aware memory modeling  
- **Storage Planning** based on growth, replication & backup strategy  
- **Network Bandwidth Estimation** with latency, scope, and QoS constraints  
- **Accelerator Detection** (GPU, TPU, NPU, or None)  
- **AWS Instance Recommendation** using XGBoost-trained price prediction model  
- **Professional PDF Report Generation** for enterprise sharing  

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

User Input (Natural Language)
↓
FAISS + LLM Agent Classifiers
↓
Agents (Workload → Concurrency → SMT → RAM → Storage → Bandwidth)
↓
XGBoost-based AWS Price Predictor
↓
PDF Report Generator (ReportLab)


---

## ⚙️ Tech Stack

- **LangChain Agents + Groq LLaMA 3**  
- **FAISS** for semantic classification  
- **XGBoost** for cost prediction  
- **OpenAI Embeddings (text-embedding-ada-002)**  
- **Streamlit** frontend  
- **ReportLab** for PDF generation  
- **Joblib + Scikit-learn** for ML models  

---

## 📦 Repository Contents

| File / Folder        | Description |
|----------------------|-------------|
| `sample.py`          | Main Streamlit app with all agent workflows |
| `*.pkl`              | Trained models (e.g., pricing, labels) |
| `*.index`            | FAISS vector indexes for workload/app type |
| `model_feature_order.pkl` | Required feature ordering for ML model |
| `enhanced_aws_pricing_model.pkl` | Trained XGBoost regressor for price prediction |

---

